## What we do

We design and test our website to meet the **Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, level AA**. This is the standard used by the UK government.

You should be able to:

- make text up to **200% bigger** without text spilling off the screen
- use the whole website with **just a keyboard**
- use the website with a **screen reader** such as VoiceOver, TalkBack or NVDA
- use **voice control** software
- see your device's **dark mode**, if you have it switched on
- turn off animations by switching on **reduce motion** on your device
- **print** any page, including your self-check results

We also:

- write in **plain English**, with short sentences and no jargon where we can avoid it
- use a font designed to be **easy to read**, including for people with low vision
- use colours with **strong contrast**
- make buttons and links **large enough to tap** easily on a phone
- never rely on colour alone to show meaning

## How accessible this website is

We believe this website fully meets WCAG 2.2 level AA. We are not aware of any parts that are hard to use. If you find one, please tell us.

## Tell us about a problem

If you find something on our website hard to use, or you need information in a different format, such as large print or plain text, email **hello@juniperhealth.info**.

Please tell us:

- the web address (URL) of the page
- what the problem is
- what device and software you use, if you know

We will reply within **5 working days**.

## If you are not happy with our response

Under the **Equality Act 2010**, service providers must make reasonable adjustments for disabled people. If you are not happy with how we respond to an accessibility problem, you can contact the **Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS)**:

- Website: equalityadvisoryservice.com
- Telephone: 0808 800 0082

## How we test this website

We test our pages with automated tools and by hand, including checking keyboard use, zoom and screen readers on phones and computers. We test again whenever we add new types of page.

This statement was prepared on 25 September 2026.
